$ Two unsymmetric CBAR cantilevers (I12 not zero) with shear factors K1, K2 and a tip force in Y and Z.
$ Elements 1-2: L = 100 mm, A = 4E-4, I1 = 2E-8, I2 = 1E-8, I12 = 5E-9. Elements 3-4: the same scaled by 1E-4.
$ The small bar's I12 = 5E-25 m^4 is smaller than machine epsilon but is a real value that must be used as is,
$ so both bars are treated the same, with no shear deformation (Mystran ignores K1, K2 when I12 is not zero).
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = 101_bar_small_i12
ECHO = NONE
SPC = 1
LOAD = 1
DISPLACEMENT = ALL
SPCFORCES = ALL
STRESS = ALL
ELFORCE = ALL
BEGIN BULK
PARAM,POST,-1
MAT1,1,2.E+11,,0.3,0.,0.,0.0
PBAR,1,1,0.0004,2.E-08,1.E-08,2.E-08,,,+P1
+P1,0.01,0.01,-0.01,0.01,-0.01,-0.01,0.01,-0.01,+Q1
+Q1,0.8333333,0.8333333,5.E-09,
GRID,1,,0.,0.,0.0
GRID,2,,0.05,0.,0.0
GRID,3,,0.1,0.,0.0
CBAR,1,1,1,2,0.0,1.0,0.0
CBAR,2,1,2,3,0.0,1.0,0.0
FORCE,1,3,,100.,0.0,2.0,1.0
PBAR,2,1,4.E-12,2.E-24,1.E-24,2.E-24,,,+P2
+P2,1.E-06,1.E-06,-1.E-06,1.E-06,-1.E-06,-1.E-06,1.E-06,-1.E-06,+Q2
+Q2,0.8333333,0.8333333,5.E-25,
GRID,4,,0.,1.,0.0
GRID,5,,5.E-06,1.,0.0
GRID,6,,1.E-05,1.,0.0
CBAR,3,2,4,5,0.0,1.0,0.0
CBAR,4,2,5,6,0.0,1.0,0.0
FORCE,1,6,,1.E-06,0.0,2.0,1.0
SPC1,1,123456,1,4
ENDDATA
